        <mxCell id="ucNote" value="Confirming a handover joins two actors on purpose.

The courier asks for the parcel and the shop answers. Neither can complete it alone — which is the whole point, and the project’s answer to logistics being &quot;organized manually between sellers and courier services&quot;." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#eef2ff;strokeColor=#4f46e5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4338ca;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="970" width="320" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ucLegend" value="Amber cases are performed by more than one kind of account.

Every other colour is the one the application itself uses: customer indigo, shop purple, courier emerald, administrator slate." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
